{
  "note": "Settings of the Civil 3D probe round (R150 to R159). Every ROSHN file name, layer name and surface name the c3d_*.py files use sits here. accoreconsole is the core console of Civil 3D 2026 and product the switch that loads Civil 3D in it. probeDll is the .NET 8 build of dotnet/SiteAdaptation.C3DProbe/Civil, relative to the repo root. sourceRoot holds the real drawings, folders names the folders copied into probeRoot/work with their layout kept, so xrefs resolve. Nothing is ever written under sourceRoot. probeRoot holds work, out and logs, outside the repo. drawings gives each drawing of the round a short role and its path under work. timeoutSeconds is how long one core console run may take before the runner stops the process it started. survey holds what python/c3d_drawings.py looks for in the ACadSharp output of each copy (R154): levelWords are words that mark a level text, levelRange the band a bare number must fall in to look like a level, levelDecimals the least decimals it must have, and lineRoles the layer patterns, matched without case, of the lines that may be a curb, an edge of road, a back of sidewalk, a right of way, a building line or a setback. connect holds what python/c3d_connect.py reads to tie the drawings to the plots (R156 to R158). baseplanPlots and landxmlDir are earlier reader outputs on this machine, plan and prototypes the answer key of the past job. curb names the drawing role and layers of the curb lines the plot front is taken from. lines names the other line sets to measure, and backOfSidewalk which of them stands for the back of the sidewalk. searchM is how far a surface edge is looked for, textRadiusM and lineRadiusM how near a level text or a 3D line must be to give a level. bandsM are the 5 mm and 30 mm bands. neighbourhoods names the schedule and plot number shift of each neighbourhood, null where none is on this machine. unitPlotTypes are the baseplan types that carry a unit. cutPlots are the plots whose cut is checked against the footprint blocks of cutDrawing, cutLabels the baseplan labels and types of that cut. snapM is how far outside its last triangle a point may lie and still take the level of the nearest surface edge (R157). surfacePair are the two surfaces whose overlap python/c3d_surfaces.py samples on a grid of overlapStepM (R155). checkSurface is the surface whose snapped level python/c3d_check.py recomputes by brute force (R159). dataBook holds round DATA (R160 to R168): root is the data book outside the repo with its own work copies of folders, drawings gives each drawing a role and its path under work, border names the drawing, layer and label of the Phase 1 border (R163), acad and watcher are the full Civil 3D window and the dialog watcher of R161, minFreeGB stops a run when free memory falls under it, timeoutMinutes ends a run that takes longer, knownSurfaces are the surfaces of the existing LandXML that are not exported again, unless exportKnownSurfaces is true, then the full window exports every surface (R169), roadSurfaceOrder is the order surfaces are asked for the plot front level (R166), excel is the master plan workbook, schedules and coordinate PDFs come from the earlier readers. dataBook.join names what python/data_book.py joins per plot (R166): fallbackOutputs are earlier CadReader outputs used where a data book table holds no geometry, cutsheet the frame and number layers, footprint the drawing and the setback layer, curb and row the line layers, v9 the plot number text layer, masterBlocks the drawings whose blocks are read per plot, unitsRev6 the unit count of Rev 6 the plot count is compared with. dataBook.locationPlan holds Part L of round DATA-2 (R179 to R183), what python/location_plan.py reads from the Zone 4 location plan: pdf the copy under root/work, outFolder its rows in the data book, labelSize the font size band of the plot labels, joinGapPt and lineTolerancePt how characters join into a text line, patterns the kinds a line is classed as in that order, codeKinds the kinds that pair with a number under them within pairDyPt and pairDxPt, fitNeighbourhood the plots the page is fitted to the site on, fitDropFactor, fitRounds and fitFloorM the robust fit, formOfSuffix the typology form each label suffix names in the old to new code table, sales, codeTable and dlus the Rev 9 sheets, zoneStyles the stroke colour and width of the zone outlines of the key plan, zoneHatch the hatch of the plan and how near a label must be to count under it, controlSearchPt and controlShapeMaxPt where the mark of a control point is looked for, check the neighbourhood, seeds, sample size and character window of python/location_plan_check.py (R184), searchWords the words looked for in every text. dataBook.wiring holds Part W of round DATA-2 (R174 to R178), what python/wiring.py tries and scores: pdfFolder the PDF reader output under root, shiftSearch and pdfToleranceM the shift search and edge tolerance of R28 and R24, unitBlockKinds the unit block names, r06Outlines a CadReader run on the R06 copy for its block outlines, widenM the widening of the fixed footprint join, minShare and shareTie the least share and the tie of the share methods, ownerShareMin the share a setback line needs in one face to belong to it, nearestM and tieM the nearest method, labelNearM the type and label match, answerShareMin the share of a past generic floor that names its face and its block in the answer key, frontToleranceM the agreement of a curb or ROW distance, levelMethods, nearestVertexM and levelToleranceM the road level methods, labelLayer the baseplan label layer, blockOverlapMin the overlap over union of two block outlines of two drawings, baseCurb the second curb, curbStepM and curbBandsM how the two curbs are compared, current the method R166 used per source, kept on a tie, chosen the method per source data_book.py wires with, check the seeds, sample size, grid step, share slack, least front edge, distance slack and the most grid points per outline of python/wiring_check.py (R178). dataBook.retest holds round DATA-2 (R170 to R173): steepUnits are the Rev 6 units the by typology test gives the steepest front slope of the profile, unitBlockKinds the first word of a footprint unit block name, unitShareMin the share of a block outline a face must hold to carry one of its units, setbackLinesM the drawn setback distances the second method classes by, check the seeds, sample size, least front edge and length slack of python/data_book_retest_check.py, phase1Sheet the rows and columns of the Phase1 sheet the units are compared with, unitsRev6ByCode the Rev 6 count by unit code. dataBook.analysis holds what python/data_book_analysis.py compares with (R167): the plot widths of Rev 6 by client plot type, widthFromCad the client types whose width comes from CAD and is no conflict (VL4, Bader in round DATA-2), the setback of Rev 6 (5.52 m, C10 5.50 m) with their tolerances, the client types that carry a unit, the neighbourhood codes searched in every text and the level bands.",
